<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Injected as /System/Installation/Packages/OSInstall.collection, and named
  by minstallconfig.xml's Package key.

  A collection is a list of packages the installer installs in order, so
  the OS and anything that should be part of it go in one pass. THIS IS
  WHERE THE FIRST-BOOT PAYLOAD BELONGS: build it as a .pkg, drop it beside
  OSInstall.mpkg, and add a line here. That installs it as part of the
  install rather than injecting it into a finished volume afterwards,
  which is what the plan's Task 6 assumes and is worse.

  OSInstall.mpkg IS LISTED TWICE, AND THAT IS NOT A TYPO. Upstream
  (timsutton/osx-vm-templates) does the same, and it reads like a
  copy/paste slip, so the first version of this file listed it once. That
  install failed with "There was a problem with the automated
  installation" before writing one byte to the target volume; putting the
  second entry back is what made it run. See the P4 Task 5 entry in
  NOTES.md.

  Additional packages go after these two.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<array>
	<string>/System/Installation/Packages/OSInstall.mpkg</string>
	<string>/System/Installation/Packages/OSInstall.mpkg</string>
</array>
</plist>
